[Applause]  suicide drone in action they've  bombarded Ukraine in recent weeks  [Music]  here police shoot one out the sky  Iran is accused of selling many of this  kind of drone to Russia  it claims it was only a small number  supplied before the war  but a Security Source has told Sky News  of a secret deal that allegedly involved  Moscow flying 140 million euros to Iran  in August in return for more than 160  drones  it wasn't just cash allegedly on the  Russian aircraft The Source said Russia  had managed to get hold of a shipment of  UK and U.S weapons that had been  intended for the ukrainians within that  captured shipment The Source said three  different weapons anti-tank and  anti-aircraft missiles were also  transported to Iran the fear is the  Iranians could try to reverse engineer  them and develop models of Their Own  The Source also shared these satellite  images allegedly showing two Russian  ilyushin il-76 aircraft marked here at  an airport in Tehran at least one was  allegedly involved in the mission  Sky News can't independently verify the  two aircraft as Russian  but we have geolocated the images to an  area on the western side of mehrabad  airport in the Iranian Capital comparing  the images with one we obtained  ourselves from the previous day we can  match up the shapes of these two hangars  the runway here and the boundary  it's also possible to see these two  other aircraft parked at the same place  in the same location  the two allegedly Russian planes are  first pictured at 1 17 am local time on  the 20th of August  by just after 3 30 a.m one of them has  moved to the runway side and the other  has turned around  in the final image three and a half  hours later they can no longer be seen  Ukraine isn't just worried about Iran's  Shahid 136 suicide drones  what we are afraid is the reports of  much more sophisticated ballistic  missiles that's around about to sell to  Russia this still have to be  investigated but this will cause a real  real threat Iran has denied the  allegation  as for Russia its previously dismissed  claims it's using Iranian drones in  Ukraine but the Security Source claimed  a new deal was finalized just a few days  ago  if true it could bring more pain from  the skies  debraham Sky News

